@startuml

salt
{
  <b>ONBOARD A PARTY AND VERIFY ITS CONVENTIONS</b>  { Plan | Publish | What the party holds }
  --
  {
    {
      <b>The plan's step, and the bundle it names</b>
      --
      {#
        Step | Operation | Argument
        ... | import_lei_hierarchy | {"bundles": ["acme_lei_import"]}
        <b>30</b> | <b>provision_party</b> | {"bundles": ["party_essentials"]}
        40 | load_staff | (the four operational parties)
      }
      --
      <b>party_essentials</b>, published once per party with {"party_id": "..."}
      {#
        Order | Member
        <b>5</b> | <b>ore.conventions</b>  (the instrument conventions)
        20 | refdata.crm_topology_bundles
      }
      <i>The conventions are a step of provisioning. They are not a manual fill.</i>
      [ Read the run ]
    } | {
      <b>The publish step, with its four counts</b>
      --
      refdata.v1.ops.publish_conventions_from_dq, party id in the params
      {#
        Party | inserted | updated | skipped
        ACMCOR, the first | <b>2,188</b> | 0 | 0
        ACCOUK, ACCOUS, ACCOHK, each | <b>2,155</b> | 0 | <b>33</b>
      }
      --
      <b>The 33, accounted for</b>
      2,188 = 2,155 party rows + 33 tenant rows.
      ibor_index 10 + overnight_index 23 = 33. They carry no party_id, so the
      guard "not already here for this tenant and party" finds the row the first
      party's publish wrote. Every later party reads 33 skipped, correctly.
      <b>Already present, tenant-wide. Not a failure.</b>
      --
      <b>How the four tenant kinds arrived</b>
      {#
        Kind | Rows | Written by
        currency_pair | 179 | the base bundle, per tenant, before any party
        overnight_index | 23 | the first party's publish
        ibor_index | 10 | the first party's publish
        tenor | 4 | ores_iam_provision_tenant_fn, once per tenant, never after
      }
    }
  }
  --
  {
    {
      <b>What the party holds, and what a run would write</b>
      --
      {#
        Scope | Kinds | Rows | Owner
        the party's own | 22 | <b>2,155</b> | ACCOUS
        shared with the tenant | 4 | <b>216</b> | the tenant
        <b>what a run writes</b> | 26 | <b>2,371</b> | the party's whole document
      }
      <i>The party's own count and the number of documents its run reads are different numbers.</i>
      <i>The four configuration names its definitions bind do not enter into it.</i>
      [ See the conventions... ]
    } | {
      <b>Verified</b>
      --
      {#
        Kind | Rows | Owner | Provenance of the row
        swap | 320 | party | system.external_data_import
        deposit | 163 | party | system.external_data_import
        currency_pair | 179 | tenant | system.external_data_import
        tenor | 4 | tenant | system.new_record, copied at provisioning
      }
      [ Change a kind... ]
      --
      <b>Unpublished</b>  (a party the bundle never reached)
      --
      <b>This party holds no conventions of its own.</b>
      It reads the tenant's 216 for the four tenant kinds, so it does not look empty.
      Its runs write a conventionsFile with no rows for the 22 party kinds.
      Nothing refuses such a run and nothing says the party was skipped.
      --
      [ Publish party_essentials for this party ]
      <i>The same operation provisioning sends. Not 2,155 hand-written rows.</i>
    }
  }
}

@enduml
